# The CI integration-suite manifest is append-only data: `merge=union` makes a
# conflicting merge concatenate BOTH branches' added lines instead of raising a
# conflict, so two PRs each adding a suite line both land with no manual
# resolution. It does not dedupe or sort, so a duplicate/reorder residue is
# possible — that is caught deterministically (never a conflict) by
# `ci_run_coverage.rs::manifest_is_sorted_and_unique`, with a copy-paste
# `LC_ALL=C sort -u` fix. See docs/changelog.d and the manifest header.
.github/ci/integration-suites.txt merge=union text eol=lf

# The manifest and runner script are checked out with LF on every OS (the runner
# is executed by Git Bash on the Windows CI leg; a CRLF-corrupted `.sh` would
# fail to parse).
.github/ci/run-suites.sh          text eol=lf
*.sh                              text eol=lf

# The generated OpenAPI document is compiled into the plugin with `include_str!`
# and served verbatim, so its bytes must not depend on the platform that built
# the binary. A CRLF checkout on Windows would serve CRLF to every client and
# break the byte-exact artifact comparison in `openapi_spec`. JSON is always
# text, so pin the whole class rather than the two files that bite today.
*.json                            text eol=lf
